BUILD-112 — did the message actually arrive? Summary.

Base tested: main at b589fa2.
CLI delivered into: Claude Code (Ink UI), v2.1.240, unauthenticated ("Not logged in - Please run /login").
Confirmed real input box present (not a plain shell) — see pane captures.

Two tenants, own container/.env per tenant, separate clones:
  default: tenant build112d-0824-1256 (PASTE_ENTER_DELAY unset -> code default 0.5s)
  zero:    tenant build112z-0824-1257 (PASTE_ENTER_DELAY=0, baked in at container start via
           container/.env + --force-recreate, confirmed via `docker exec printenv`)

Method: 50 envelopes per configuration, unique marker per envelope (MARKD001-050 /
MARKZ001-050), sent via the real `office send` CLI path (architect -> sme-2).
Interleaved: one send to default, one send to zero, repeated 50 times — never in
blocks. Sequential within each tenant (one office send call completes before the
next is issued to that same tenant), so no client-side concurrency confound.

Per-configuration counts:

  configuration          | envelopes sent | opened records | markers submitted
  PASTE_ENTER_DELAY=0.5   |       50       |       50       |        50
  PASTE_ENTER_DELAY=0     |       50       |       50       |        50

"Opened" counted by exact stream_id match against custody-{d,z}.jsonl (not by
destination+count alone, to rule out cross-contamination from earlier pilot
sends against the same tenant).

"Submitted" counted from Claude Code's own session transcript file
(~/.claude/projects/-workdir-sme-2/*.jsonl), matching {"type":"user",
"message":{"role":"user"},...} entries containing the marker — this is the CLI's
own record of a turn it actually processed, not a screen-scrape. A message
merely pasted-and-unsubmitted never produces this record, since the CLI never
receives a submit event for it. Cross-checked against tmux capture-pane for
the visible tail (see pane-d.txt / pane-z.txt) — consistent for the markers
still visible there.

Result: ZERO submissions lost at either configuration, across 50 envelopes each,
verified by marker identity (no gaps: comm -23 against the full 001-050 set
returned empty for both configurations).

Side observation, OUT OF SCOPE for this measurement, not included in the counts
above: five markers sent CONCURRENTLY (backgrounded, not serialized) to the
zero-delay tenant during calibration showed real corruption — two markers
coalesced into a single submitted turn, and one marker (BURSTZ003) never
appeared anywhere in the pane or scrollback. This is a client-concurrency
collision, a different variable than ENTER_DELAY's paste-vs-Enter timing, and
was not pursued further here.
